      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>To promote international friendship, peace, and cross-cultural understanding through educational programs, youth engagement, public diplomacy, and cultural exchange. The organization achieves its mission by developing afterschool enrichment programs, facilitating student-led global initiatives, hosting cultural festivals and civic receptions, and fostering people-to-people connections between San Diego and its sister cities, particularly Yokohama, Japan.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Connect the World Afterschool Program ($155,717.83 expenses | $12,410 grant) Delivered Japanese language and cultural enrichment classes at Crown Point Junior Music Academy, Doyle Elementary, and partner campuses, serving over 75 students. Activities included bilingual instruction, intercultural projects, and virtual exchanges with sister schools in Yokohama. Covered payroll, classroom rentals, supplies, insurance, and digital subscriptions. The program builds global citizenship and youth leadership through cross-cultural learning.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>12410</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>155718</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Youth &amp; Educational Leadership Programs (Meraki / SD-WISH) ($36,382 expenses | $12,410 grant) Included the Mission Bay High School Jazz Preservationists goodwill tour to Yokohama, the Kanazawa High School exchange visit to San Diego, the Meraki Concert Series Work-Study Program, and SD-WISHs Peace &amp; Humanity Day. Students gained practical experience in music, event management, and cultural diplomacy while promoting peace, collaboration, and mutual understanding.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>12410</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>36382</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Educational Exchange &amp; Teacher Programs ($12,273.17 expenses | $0 grants) Supported bilateral school and teacher exchanges between San Diego and Yokohama, including classroom visits, virtual collaborations, and professional development workshops. Strengthened international educational partnerships and deepened intercultural understanding among educators and students.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>12273</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
