    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="ScheduleO" documentName="IRS990ScheduleO">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part I, Line 16</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The total reported under Line 16 reflects program-related and operational expenses that supported the organizations mission of cultural exchange, international friendship, and educational outreach. These expenses were primarily tied to the planning, execution, and delivery of the following initiatives: Connect the World Afterschool Program: Provided Japanese language and cultural enrichment at Crown Point Junior Music Academy, Doyle Elementary, and other sites, serving over 75 students. Covered payroll, classroom rentals, supplies, digital subscriptions, insurance, and student snacks. Otsukimi Moon Viewing Festival (September 2024): Organized a large-scale community celebration of the Japanese moon-viewing tradition, featuring sumo demonstrations, taiko performances, traditional dance, yukata rentals, food vendors, and educational booths. Over 500 attendees participated. Indigenous Sustainable Design Forum (November 2024): Hosted in partnership with UC San Diego Global Initiatives, the event brought together Indigenous leaders to share perspectives on sustainability, VR storytelling, art, and cultural ceremony. Kanazawa High School Student Visit (March 2025): Welcomed visiting students from Yokohamas Kanazawa High School as part of the Sister School exchange program with Mission Bay High School. Activities included classroom exchanges, cultural experiences, and collaborative projects promoting cross-cultural understanding. Mission Bay High School Jazz Preservationists Tour (April 2025): Coordinated the student goodwill ambassadorial tour to Yokohama, Japan, where Mission Bay High Schools Jazz Preservationists performed at sister city and community venues, promoting friendship and mutual understanding through music. Meraki Concert Series (20242025): Produced in partnership with Mission Bay High Schools Jazz Program, this student-led concert series provided hands-on experience in event production, marketing, and music business operations, while raising funds for cultural exchange programs. Yokohama Teacher Exchange Visits (July 2024 &amp; May 2025): Hosted teacher delegations from Yokohama, Japan, providing classroom observations, school tours, professional workshops, and cultural exchange opportunities to strengthen educational collaboration. General operational costs include subscriptions to Zoom, Adobe, QuickBooks accounting software, MembershipWorks, website-related plugins and integrations, banking fees, storage rentals, printing, and insurance.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
